<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2812" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀΐω</span></b>  (A), 
			Ep.
		 and Lyr. word, freq. used by Trag. in lyr., cf. <i><span class="en">
			Hermipp.
			47.7
		</span></i> (anap.); once only in dialogue (<i><span class="en">
			S.
			<u>OC</u>
			304
		</span></i>): only pres. and impf. (aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ-ήϊσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					9.93
				</span></i>
			):—<i>perceive</i> by the ear, <i>hear</i>, c.
			acc. rei, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἀΐεις ἅ τέ φησι;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.130
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				248
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νέστωρ δὲ πρῶτος κτύπον ἄϊε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					10.532
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				21.388
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>Pae.</u>
				6.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				55
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.</u>
				59
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				148
			</span></i>, etc.: c. gen.rei, <i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
				1.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				304
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1410
			</span></i>: c. gen. pers., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀΐει μου . . βασιλεύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					633
				</span></i>
			;—also, <i>perceive</i> by the eye, <i>see</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				181
			</span></i>:—generally, <i>perceive</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἀΐεις ὡς Τρῶες . . ἥαται ἄγχι
					νεῶν;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					10.160
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. gen.,
				<i>listen to, give ear to</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίκης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					213
				</span></i>
			 (dub. l.); <i>obey</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				874
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				1166
			</span></i>. (Cf. Skt. <i>āvis</i> 'clear', Lat.
			<i>au-dio.</i>) [<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> uses <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ</span> always in
				pres., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰῐω</span>; so <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				633
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1410
			</span></i>; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱῐεις</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ᾱῐων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					59
				</span></i>
			 (prob.), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				181
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				304
			</span></i>: impf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱῐε</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				10.532
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				21.38
			</span></i>&lt;*&gt; (as always in Trag.), but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰῐεν</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.463
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰῐον</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				18.222
			</span></i>:—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ι</span> is always short,
			except <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰῑε</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				213
			</span></i> (dub. <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>.), and perh. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀϊόντεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.352
				</span></i>
			.]</div>
